\n**The verify suite is green for this change. CI exit status: SUCCESS (0).**\n\n- Change: Gerrit 2993, patch set 1, revision `396225b395b4e127eca37017f91eee89c509a553`\n- CI run: https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/35488610331\n- Verdict: `rebar-ci-bot` cast **`Verified +1` — SUCCESS**, every job green (lint +\n  type-check, the `ubuntu-latest, py3.13` gating pytest cell and the rest of the matrix,\n  sandbox enforcement, mutation, artifact-probe, authorship, optionality,\n  scanner-integration).\n- Landed: submitted revision-scoped and merged to `main`.\n\n`AGENTS.md` defines `make test` as selecting exactly what CI's gating `ubuntu-latest, py3.13`\ncell selects, and describes a local `make verify` as \"the locally checkable **half** of\n`Verified`\". CI ran that selection plus the rest of the matrix and passed, so this is the\nstronger of the two signals.","timestamp":1789882808864006218},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion gate returned FAIL at 2026-09-19T23:2x — investigated before re-running, and the FAIL was not about this ticket's criteria.\n\nThe gate was started without an explicit `ref`, so it verified against the store repository's checked-out HEAD (`e900fa14ad5`, 2026-09-19 00:40 UTC) rather than current `origin/main`. This ticket's fix merged as `9f67fcfef7a`, which is reachable from `origin/main` but **not** from that stale HEAD, so the \"work landed\" precheck failed before any criteria were judged.\n\nConfirming evidence: zero `COMPLETION_VERDICT` events were written to this ticket's directory. A real criteria judgement always writes one with a per-criterion `met` array. The control is `16c9-a42d` and `5a31-8c91`, verified in the same session with an explicit `ref` — both PASSed and both recorded a verdict.\n\nRe-running now with `ref=d5c325a4170dfee29af010164a1cc2e3289cdc83`. The description and acceptance criteria were not changed, because nothing about them was implicated.\n\nThe misleading failure shape is filed separately as `selective-dermic-coelacanth` (c6fb-49cf).","timestamp":1789886952088861488},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"**Correction — my previous comment on this ticket was wrong.** The stale-store-HEAD diagnosis does not hold, and the FAIL is genuine.\n\nI tested it and it was refuted three ways: `--ref` defaults to `origin/main` (not the store HEAD) per `rebar verify-completion --help`; re-running with an explicit `ref=d5c325a4170` still FAILed; and `16c9-a42d` / `5a31-8c91`, which PASSed, are equally unreachable from that stale HEAD and equally record `file_impact`. Disregard the earlier comment.\n\n**The actual root cause: change 2993 satisfied 4 of 5 codebase criteria but missed one.** Criterion c01 requires `docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md` to mention that `pyproject.toml:353-356` pins the required uv version to `==0.12.7`. The doc does mention uv 0.12.7 at line 75 (prerequisites), but never cites `pyproject.toml` as the source of the pin — searching the file for `pyproject.toml` and `required-version` returned no matches.\n\nVerifier findings at `ref=d5c325a4170dfee29af010164a1cc2e3289cdc83`: 2 unmet criteria, both `severity: high` — c01 itself, and the derived \"bug is actually resolved\" criterion. The `pip install .[agents,reviewbot]` replacement, the four-service topology, the host-side nginx statement, and the ADR 0007 preservation all passed, as did the `[non-codebase]` verify-suite criterion.\n\n**Remediation in flight.** Worktree `fix-1d89-uv-pin-ref` at `origin/main`. The section-5 compose paragraph now reads `uv sync --locked --no-dev --extra agents --extra reviewbot --extra bedrock`, with `pyproject.toml:353-356` pinning the required uv version to `==0.12.7`. Confirmed against the tree first: `required-version = \"==0.12.7\"` sits at `pyproject.toml:356`, inside the cited range. `make verify` running; Gerrit change to follow.\n\nThe async surface's failure to expose these findings is filed as `selective-dermic-coelacanth` (c6fb-49cf).","timestamp":1789887483740983718},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"**Addendum — which tree the verifier actually read.**\n\nMy previous comment said the findings came from `ref=d5c325a4170`. They did not. The MCP workspace at `/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code` was checked out at `8f7417079a` (2026-09-19 02:18 UTC), 28.5 hours behind `main`, and every completion run read that tree regardless of the `ref` passed. Change 2993's merge commit `9f67fcfef7a` is **not** an ancestor of `8f7417079a`, so the verifier could not see this ticket's fix at all. Filed on `working-carnelian-bobwhite` (8806-198c) with the measurements.\n\n**The conclusion is unchanged, and I re-confirmed it directly rather than relying on the verifier.** Against the current tip of `main`:\n\n```\ngit show origin/main:docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md | grep -n 'pyproject.toml\\|required-version'\n(no matches)\n```\n\nNeither `pyproject.toml` nor `required-version` appears anywhere in the file at `origin/main`, so criterion c01 — the doc must cite `pyproject.toml:353-356` as the source of the `==0.12.7` uv pin — is genuinely unmet and the remediation in flight is still required.\n\nNet: the FAIL verdict was right, its stated reasoning was about the wrong tree, and the underlying gap is real. I will re-verify with `ref=origin/main` once the follow-up change merges.","timestamp":1789888174624515265}],"created_at":1788594869468850001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d6b66461-736d-49cd-8ec9-32656cb9920f","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"a0f1-b86c-5199-4a42"},{"link_uuid":"32a28827-0a5a-40e9-bade-415af1c62da0","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7a8f-5915-0735-4717"},{"link_uuid":"b09a24c9-8275-42d8-84ac-f2cd0ada7a79","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f29d-9fe3-e35f-4f49"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md:72-74` says the review-bot image installs the `nava-rebar[agents]` extra with `pip install .[agents,reviewbot]`. `docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md:211-215` says the compose stack runs two containers, Gerrit and review-bot, and repeats the `pip install .[agents,reviewbot]` install shape.\n\nThe current image build uses locked uv, not a bare pip install. `infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot:93-100` pins uv through `ghcr.io/astral-sh/uv:0.12.7` and runs `uv sync --locked --no-dev --extra agents --extra reviewbot --extra bedrock`; `pyproject.toml:353-356` pins `[tool.uv] required-version = \"==0.12.7\"`.\n\nThe current compose file defines four services, not two: `gerrit` at `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:27`, `review-bot` at `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:76`, `opcert` at `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:346`, and `mcp` at `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:418`. nginx remains host-side and outside compose; the service comments describe host nginx proxying to the loopback-published service ports at `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:37-38`, `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:279-280`, `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:394-395`, and `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:407-410`.\n\n## Approach\nUpdate `docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md` to match the current review-bot Dockerfile and compose topology. Leave historical ADR prose unchanged unless the referenced lines are part of the operator guide statements above.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md` removes the review-bot prerequisite claim at lines 72-74 that the image bakes `pip install .[agents,reviewbot]` and replaces it with the locked install from `infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot:98-100`: uv `0.12.7` running `uv sync --locked --no-dev --extra agents --extra reviewbot --extra bedrock`.\n- [x] `docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md` replaces the repeated `pip install .[agents,reviewbot]` claim at line 213 with the same locked uv install and mentions that `pyproject.toml:353-356` pins the required uv version to `==0.12.7`.\n- [x] `docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md` removes the two-container topology claim at lines 211-212 and replaces it with the four compose services from `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`: `gerrit`, `review-bot`, `opcert`, and `mcp`.\n- [x] `docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md` keeps nginx described as host-side and outside compose, with nginx proxying to loopback-published service ports rather than listed as a compose service.\n- [x] `docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md` leaves historical ADR 0007 wording unchanged outside the current operator-guide drift at lines 72-74 and 211-215.\n- [x] [non-codebase] The full verify suite is green for this change, with the run and its\n      exit code recorded on this ticket. The authoritative signal is the Gerrit `Verified`\n      vote on this change's patch set, which runs the same selection `make test` runs.\n      provenance: environment=github-actions-hosted-runner; principal=rebar-ci-bot; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — CI run 35488610331 executed the gating suite against Gerrit change 2993 patch set 1 (revision 396225b395b4e127eca37017f91eee89c509a553) and concluded SUCCESS, casting `Verified +1`; that run is the same merge gate that admits the change to `main`, so its exit status is the authoritative verify result rather than a simulation of one.\n\n## Testing\nRun `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify` from the repository checkout and land only if it exits 0.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md","reason":"Align the operator guide's review-bot install and compose-topology statements with the locked uv Dockerfile and four-service compose stack."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","7a8f-5915-0735-4717"],["relates_to","f29d-9fe3-e35f-4f49"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"63d07776-8f49-41